# Intro
A single, fixed-mass star at the centre of a uniform, periodic glass-IC gas
box, with photoelectric heating on but ISRF propagation off
(photoionization and radiation pressure also off). The example checks the
injection step of the ISRF alone: at `Z=0` there is no dust extinction, so the
energy injected into all gas particles that the star reaches must equal
`Delta_t * L_band`:

```
sum_j(PESpecificEnergies_j * mass_j) == Delta_t * PELuminosities_star
sum_j(LWSpecificEnergies_j  * mass_j) == Delta_t * LWLuminosities_star
```

`Delta_t` is the feedback time step of the star at the checked snapshot. The
luminosities and `Delta_t` are read from the snapshot and from `output.log`.

`ISRF_propagation: 0` keeps the packet transport from moving energy between
particles. Each star feedback pass then resets and re-injects the specific
energies, so the last snapshot holds one injection pass.
`run.sh` passes `--cooling`, and `GrackleCooling:disable_cooling_for_debugging: 1`
in `params.yml` skips the cooling update, so the example needs no thermal
evolution.

## Metallicity
`initial_metallicity: 0` in `params.yml` is the default leg.
`metallicity=<Z> ./run.sh` runs the same box at a nonzero metal mass fraction
(absolute, not solar: `run.sh` turns `scale_initial_metallicity` off with it)
and switches the check to the extinction identities (see Checking).
`metallicity=0.01295` is Grackle's solar metal mass fraction. The check prints
`tau_LW`, the LW optical depth of the receiving particles.

# Configure
```
./configure --with-chemistry=GEAR_10 --with-feedback=GEAR --with-cooling=grackle_1 --with-stars=GEAR --with-sink=GEAR --with-star-formation=GEAR --with-tracers=GEAR --with-kernel=wendland-C2 --with-grackle=path/to/grackle
make -j
```
The GEAR feedback module registers the `PESpecificEnergies`/`LWSpecificEnergies`
snapshot output.

The radiation table is the stellar evolution table with the `Data/Radiation`
group. The pychem table generator produces it from its parameter file
`params/chimieparam_radiation_parsec_spectral_popII.py`; `run.sh` fetches the
published one.

# Run
```
./run.sh
```
Override any parameter via the matching env var: gas density
(`gas_density`, atom/cm^3), gas particle mass (`gas_mass`, Msun), star mass
and type (`star_mass`, `star_type`), resolution level (`level`, N =
`(2**level)**3` gas particles), run duration and stepping (`time_end`,
`dt_max`, `delta_time`), and thread count (`n_threads`); see `run.sh` for
the full list and defaults. `run_name=<dir> ./run.sh` moves the run's
outputs into `<dir>` once done, to keep more than one run's outputs side by
side.

# Checking
```
python3 isrf_injection_conservation_check.py
```
`run.sh` runs this automatically against its own `output.log` and final
snapshot. It sums `PESpecificEnergies * mass` (and the LW equivalent)
over all illuminated gas particles and compares against `Delta_t *
PELuminosities` (`--tol`, default relative error 1e-5).

At nonzero metallicity `run.sh` passes `--dusty`, which checks two
extinction identities instead: the per-particle band ratio (gate G2) and a
bracket on the weighted mean of `exp(-tau)` (gate G1). `--dust-tol` overrides
the G2 bar, and a negative value reports the residual without gating.
`--dusty` reads `GEARFeedback:ISRF_extinction_path` from `used_parameters.yml`
and rebuilds that mechanism's column. `--kernel-gamma` (default Wendland C2 in
3D) and `--extinction-path <R>` apply to `constant_kernel_path`.
`temperature_capped_jeans` is refused. Without `--dusty` a nonzero metallicity
is an error. The gates and their derivation are in the script docstring.
